  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nThe main weather message today into this weekend will be much\ncooler temperatures with scattered lake effect rain showers\nthrough Saturday night. A stronger cold front will sweep across\nthe area this morning. Winds will become blustery from the\nnorthwest today through Saturday night. Lake effect cloudiness\nand lake effect rain showers will be likely downwind of the\nGreat Lake today into Saturday. High temperatures today and this\nweekend will be in the 40s and 50s. Overnight lows will be in\nthe 30s.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nNicer weather and a return of milder temperatures will start\nSunday into early next week with high pressure building in\nacross the Ohio Valley and lower Great Lakes region. High\ntemperatures will climb from the 50s into the 60s early and\nmiddle of next week. Mainly fair weather conditions are expected\nfor the first half next week. An unsettled and colder weather\npattern may develop over the Great Lakes region by late next \nweek.",
